# TypeScript, TSX and the scripts that decide what a television installs are
# text, whatever byte a string literal happens to hold.
#
# Row.tsx carried a NUL as a list separator, and one NUL costs a source file two
# separate things: `grep -r` skips the file as binary, and git shows "Binary
# files differ" in place of a diff - so neither a person nor a bot reviewing a
# change could read it.
#
# Escaping the byte is what fixes the first, and that is done at the source.
# This file fixes only the second, and that half outlives the escape: the OTHER
# side of a comparison can still carry a NUL, and a base commit is not something
# a later change can rewrite.
#
# The build and publish scripts and the manifests are in here deliberately:
# they compute the sha256s a box trusts and decide what it installs, so they are
# the files it would matter most to hide.
#
# `.ts` is also the MPEG transport-stream extension. If a real media fixture
# ever lands, give its directory a `*.ts -diff` of its own rather than dropping
# this line - a stream rendered as text is noise, a hidden source file is a hole.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.js diff
*.jsx diff
*.mjs diff
*.cjs diff
*.json diff
*.css diff
*.html diff
*.md diff
*.sh diff
*.yml diff
*.yaml diff
